abstract: "A reusable analytical framework based on Gartner's Hype Cycle for Emerging Technologies (1995) and Technology Adoption Lifecycle models. Designed to assist in positioning emerging technologies within the five-phase Hype Cycle, distinguishing hype from substance, assessing 'crossing the chasm' probability, and providing resource allocation guidance via priority matrices. This skill provides a structured analytical framework and writing style calibration. It does NOT claim to represent Gartner, Inc. or its analysts. The Hype Cycle framework was developed by Gartner; this skill is an independent implementation for analytical purposes."
